I2C driver for the GS201 SoC of the Google Pixel 7

The driver 'gs201_i2c' provides the I2c session for the slaves of one
Samsung HSI2C controller in the devices ROM. The controller is polled, in
standard or fast mode. A session reaches the one bus address of its policy,
and only if the address is listed by an 'allow' node. 'max_write' limits
the length of a write message, 1 permits the register pointer only:

! + config | bus_speed_hz: 400000
!   + allow  | bus_address: 0x25
!   + policy | label_prefix: exynos_usb_gadget | bus_address: 0x25
!            | max_write: 2

The clocks of the controller are provided by 'gs201_platform', its pins by
'gs201_pio'. The logic without Genode dependencies is in 'hsi2c.h', with
host tests:

! make -C repos/pixel/src/driver/i2c/gs201/test

The scenario 'run/gs201_i2c_pixel' reads the ID of the Type-C controller of
the MAX77759 on the bus of USI13:

! make run/gs201_i2c_pixel KERNEL=hw BOARD=google_pixel7
